@startuml session-state
title P2P Sync — Session Lifecycle (per peer)

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Idle

Idle --> Connecting : user taps "Sync now"\n(dial last_address)
Connecting --> Authenticating : socket open\n(hello / challenge / auth / auth_ok)
Authenticating --> Pulling : auth_ok verified\nsession keys derived

Pulling --> ApplyingPull : changes_done received
ApplyingPull --> Pushing : all batches applied\n+ cursor persisted\n+ apply_ack sent
Pushing --> Complete : peer's apply_ack received\nsync_complete sent

Complete --> Idle : update last_synced_at\nemit "Pulled X, pushed Y,\nN conflicts resolved"

Connecting --> Failed : timeout / refused\n(host offline or address stale)
Authenticating --> Failed : bad MAC / unknown_peer\n/ protocol_version
Pulling --> Failed : disconnect
ApplyingPull --> Failed : disconnect / apply error\n(transaction rolls back)
Pushing --> Failed : disconnect

Failed --> Idle : surface error to Sync screen

note right of ApplyingPull
  The ONLY state that moves the cursor —
  and only in the same transaction as the
  final applied batch. Every other exit
  leaves cursors untouched, so any re-entry
  re-requests the same delta and re-applies
  idempotently. Crash-safe at every arrow.
end note

note bottom of Pushing
  Push mirrors Pull with roles swapped:
  the peer walks its own
  Pulling -> ApplyingPull path.
  A drop here means data flowed one way;
  cursors record exactly that, and the
  next session completes the other side.
end note

@enduml
